(As an example, a simple file to approximate the D.E. y'= 1/y using Euler\'s method is )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(found. To execute the commands in the file, the step size and the initia\l value must )Tj
T*
(be specified. Once done, you can easily approximate the given D.E. for a\ wide )Tj
T*
(variey of initial conditions and step sizes. )Tj
0 -2.55714 TD
(First, you will need to create the file. The easiest editor on our syste\m is to just use )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(the built in matlab editor. It will allow you to do some very simple fil\e )Tj
T*
(manipulations. The editor is very simple and easy to start. It is not a \very advanced )Tj
T*
(editor, though. )Tj
0 -2.55714 TD
(Matlab executable files \(called M-files\) must have the extension ".m".\ In this )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(example a file called simpleEuler.m is created. To get Matlab to execute\ the )Tj
T*
(commands in the file simply type in "simpleEuler". Matlab will then sear\ch the )Tj
T*
(current directory for the file "simpleEuler", read the file, and execute\ the commands )Tj
T*
(in the file. If matlab cannot find the file you will get an error messag\e: )Tj
7.28349 -2.55714 Td
(??? Undefined function or variable 'simpleEuler'. )Tj
-7.28349 -2.55714 Td
(If this is the case then either you mistyped the name of the program, th\e program is )Tj
T*
(misnamed, or the file is located in directory that matlab does not know \about. In the )Tj
T*
(later case you have to let matlab know which directory to search. The li\st of )Tj
T*
(directories that is searched for files is called the "path." For more in\formation on )Tj
