0 -2.7048 TD
(% file: simpleEuler.m)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(% This matlab file will find the approximation to)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(% dy/dx =  1/y)Tj
T*
(% y\(0\) = starty)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%  To run this file you will first need to specify)Tj
T*
(%  the step the following:)Tj
T*
(%      h       : the step size)Tj
T*
(%      starty  : the initial value)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%  The routine will generate three vectors.  The first)Tj
T*
(%  vector is x which is the grid points starting at)Tj
T*
(%  x0=0 and have a step size h.  )Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%  The second vector is an approximation to the specified)Tj
T*
(%  D.E. )Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%  The third vector is the true solution to the D.E.)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%  If you haven't guessed, you cna use the percent sign)Tj
T*
(%  to add comments.)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
